From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Sep 2026 23:40:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: prepare the resume behind the pause

Preparing a resume seeks back for the audio lead-in and decodes the interval
again, which is most of the wait between the viewer pressing play and seeing
the picture. None of it needs them waiting: the picture is already frozen and
the resume target is the current position. Arm the preparation at the pause and
park it once ready, so play only has to release what is already held. Unpause
to first picture falls from about 600ms to 135ms.

Parking needs a stage of its own, because the preparation deadline measures
work and a pause is not work. Cancelling or recovering a preparation made
behind a pause must not start playback by itself, and a frame advance has to
retire it - the held picture outranks the step, so the display would not
change otherwise. The retained picture is re-checked on a priority-only poll,
which waits 100ms while the hold stands rather than a millisecond for the
length of the pause.

A resume is not prepared nearer the start of the file than the lead-in plus
the TrueHD settle. The earlier seek is clamped to the start there, so the
audio cannot give the lead the release needs: on a 3D film paused at 0.4-0.7 s
by the shutter-glasses add-on, every preparation went straight to the
ordinary-seek fallback, a second flush on top of its own. The lead-in is
computed in one place (ResumePrerollLeadIn) and checked before a generation
is taken, both when the pause arms the preparation and when a resume is
deferred behind its callbacks, and again in BeginResumePreroll. To check it
before a generation exists, the renderer gives its preroll lead as it stands
now (GetVideoPrerollLead), the same figure BeginVideoPreroll records. A
refusal before a generation is taken logs one line, "not prepared:
target=... within lead_in_ms=... settle_ms=...", and the pause and resume
are then plain speed changes. A refusal in BeginResumePreroll, after a
generation has been taken (a 06_12 callback seek moved the target inside
the lead, or the renderer's lead changed between the two readings), is
recovered like a failed earlier seek: an ordinary seek, which retires the
generation with a flush, since retiring it without one would leave the
video thread dropping every picture.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

