-    // Two things, both measured from the stream rather than assumed.
-    //
-    // Where the previous packet ended: on the container's timeline, not on the
-    // cumulative total. A container quantizes each timestamp to a millisecond
-    // while a 48 kHz frame lasts 10.667 ms, so measuring against the running
-    // total turns per-packet rounding into a drift that eventually crosses any
-    // fixed allowance.
-    //
-    // How far off is still the next packet: half a frame. Real ladders are not
-    // just 10 and 11 ms - this content also steps 12 - so a fixed millisecond
-    // rejects healthy audio, and it rejected all of it here. Half a frame
